    "result_text": "The change is complete and the build is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented customerCode de-duplication in `buildCustomerCode` in `OwnerRestControllerV1.java:285`.\n\nThe method already computed a base code as `<REGION>-<HASH8>` (a deterministic function of region + telephone/lastname hash). I added collision handling:\n\n- It gathers all existing owners' non-null `customerCode` values.\n- If the base code isn't taken, it's returned unchanged.\n- If it collides, it appends `-<n>` starting at `n=2`, incrementing to the smallest `n \u2265 2` that yields a value not already in use, and returns that de-duplicated code (e.g. `NSW-1A2B3C4D-2`).\n\nThis preserves the existing `toLocality` logic in `OwnerMapper` (which splits on the first `-`, so the appended suffix doesn't affect the region prefix). The full test suite passes (`BUILD SUCCESS`), including the `coreCustomerCodesStayUnique` acceptance test asserting distinct owners always receive distinct customer codes.",
